sted versions\n\n4.7.dev\n\n### System information\n\nGLES3, Direct3D12, Windows\n\n### Issue description\n\nBefore anything else, I would like to mention that the process of writing and debugging scene shaders is really not great, and the rendering team would greatly benefit from better tools (Better error messages, a setting for recompiling shaders at engine startup rather than engine build time, rudimentary compile errors within the IDE).\n\nNow to the issue:\nWhen you write any non-ascii character in GLSL shader for compatibility (`drivers\\gles3\\shaders\\scene.glsl`), you get an infuriatingly unhelpful compilation error message:\n`error C0000: syntax error, unexpected $end at token \"<EOF>\"`\nThis even happens when the respective character is part of a comment, which does not help when you try to fix the error by commenting out lines (happened to me when I was trying to refer to an algorithm by somebody named Ureña, and I swear, I wasted hours on this).\n\nIf you run the engine from the console, you get slightly more helpful errors: \n`Unicode parsing error, some characters were replaced with � (U+FFFD): Invalid unicode codepoint (ffffffb1), cannot represent as UTF-8`, but it still does not say the line, the file, the particular character (ffffffb1 means nothing), or that the characters should all be ASCII, rather than UTF-8.\n\nPotentially related: https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/61756\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nAdd this comment to `drivers\\gles3\\shaders\\scene.glsl`:\n`// ñ`\n\nrecompile and run in compatibility rendering mode.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/foll